{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1442856610,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE0MjA1MDI4NA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/229#issuecomment-142050284"},"message":"may be there could/should be a magic logic allowing for a single instance of that type to be passed but then it should get wrapped into a list","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1442856933,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE0MjA1MjMzOA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/229#issuecomment-142052338"},"message":"Hmm, I would not want to mix Constraints doc string generation logic with argparse semantics. nargs='+' will always yield a list, hence the Constraint should match that and use EnsureListOf(str).\n\nQuestion is whether argparse will run it on individual values or the entire list...","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1442857577,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE0MjA1NjgzOA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/229#issuecomment-142056838"},"message":"So it seems to want a single argument. Not sure how to do this best. The parameter itself clearly needs EnsureListOf(str) -- this is fix one. But it breaks argparse' behavior.\n\nSo from this angle it is not primarily about the docstring. It is about supporting the use case that only a single item in a (potential) container is evaluated. This might need an extension of the constraint interface.\n\nSuggestions?","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1442860277,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE0MjA2OTA1Mw==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/229#issuecomment-142069053"},"message":"unfortunately I don't \"speak\" constraints/argparse machinery yet to the degree to give a sensible suggestion... thus not sure why \"only a single item\" since ideally all the elements of the list should be evaluated to guarantee they are all str.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1442860657,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE0MjA3MDY3NQ==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/229#issuecomment-142070675"},"message":"The constraint is used a `type` in argparse. That is a callable that gets used to evaluate any single argument. In case of nargs='+' every single element in what will become a list assembled by argparse. OTOH the python API will want to make sure it gets the list right away.","files":null},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1456649578,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDE4OTgyMjQ0OA==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/229#issuecomment-189822448"},"message":"So let's get this settled. It seems that if the `paths` argument can deal with single str and list(str) equally well. The solution to this issue is:\n\n`contraints=EnsureStr() | EnsureListOf(str)`\n\nwhich leads to:\n\n```\nNAME : str or list(str), optional\n  path(s) to data content that is to be obtained. Constraints: value\n  must be a string, or value must be convertible to list(str).\n  [Default: 'SOME']\n```\n\n(for the Python docstring).\n\nThis solution doesn't require interpreting argparse logic and ensures that the Python API is fully described at the same time.\n\nI consider this base issue closed.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1456649578,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkNsb3NlZEV2ZW50NTY5NjQzMjQ2"},"status":2}]}